    "reasoning": "All six answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-80473: g_xx=-4/(2x-y)² and g_yy=-1/(2x-y)², giving -5/9 at (1,-1). q-80468: both mixed partials equal 2xy sin(x²-y²), so their sum is 4xy sin(x²-y²). q-132590: fixing y=2 gives tangent slope f_x(-π/2,2)=-2; through the stated point, z=-2x+π. q-36372: fixing y=0 gives slope f_x(2,0)=5, hence z=5x-6. q-132604: fixing x=1 gives f_y(1,0)=-1 and tangent direction (0,1,-1); the selected vector (0,-1,1) is its negative and therefore equally valid. q-71221: fixing y=1 gives f_x(-1,1)=3 and tangent direction (1,0,3), explicitly stated in the source. No grade evidence was supplied; MA evidence comes from the worked solutions.",
